=== dubnacos
"Senovir's son and Dubnacos fought over a cow. Senovir's son died. That's the whole story; nobody comes out of it looking clever." He shrugs. "Seven winters' exile. He's done three, living in a hole with the kind of men who end up in holes. He knows the shrine. He knew where the box was."
-> hub

=== grotto
"Half a day northeast, up the dry valley, where the limestone opens." He wipes his hands. "Our grandfathers' grandfathers hung their dead there, or their enemies' dead, or their gods' share of them. Nobody remembers which. People don't go there."

"Dubnacos goes there. Which tells you something about Dubnacos."
-> hub

=== lore
~ set vates_lore
[lore 30] ~ xp 20
[lore 30] You know some of this already, from your grandmother: the old peoples gave Esus his share of the battle dead, hung from the trees and the high ledges, and you don't take back what's been given. The vates sees you know it, and nods.
"Old dead, given to Esus, who takes his share from a branch. The old songs say anyone who sleeps under them dreams of falling, and anyone who steals from them falls. The druids judge that kind of theft, not the elders, and they have never judged it kindly." He smiles a little. "The songs say a great many things. But outlaws are superstitious men. They'll have stayed near the mouth, I'd guess, and kept away from the deep chambers."
-> hub

=== heal
~ heal_all; time 30
He makes you sit, cleans what needs cleaning, packs what needs packing with moss and honey, and binds it with linen. His hands are better than his manner.
"Try not to come back with more of those."
-> hub

=== idol
He goes very still. "Where was that?"
* "In a niche at the back of the grotto, under the bones." -> idol2

=== idol2
"Then it belongs to the dead, and the dead to the god." He doesn't reach for it. "I'll take it, if you give it to me. I'll carry it back and put it where it was, with the right words. Or you can keep it. Men have carried worse things for luck." He looks at you. "And some of them had luck."
* Give him the idol. -> idol_give
* "I'll keep it for now." -> hub

=== idol_give
~ take grotto_idol; xp 50; honor 5; give poultice 2
He wraps it in a white cloth and holds it like a child.
"Here. For the road." Two poultices, wrapped in leaves.
-> hub

=== tally
~ quest grotto done done
"Good." He doesn't ask how. He looks at the stick and not at you. "Take it to Vellaunos. It's his business now, and yours."
-> hub

=== druids
~ set vates_druids; known carnute_forest; xp 25
[quest judgment none] ~ quest judgment start
He's quiet a moment. "I was there. A boy holding the bowl. The Roman officer swore by his gods and Vellaunos by ours, and the druid who came down from the north took the oath away with him, the way they do." He picks at the grass. "Oaths like that are kept in the Carnute forest, where the druids of all Gaul meet once a year. North, past Cenabum. A sanctuary in the oaks."

"If Rome broke faith first, the druids can say so, and Brigodunon is free of its word. That would matter, at an assembly. Men will do a great deal with a clean conscience." He looks up. "Or the druids can say we're bound. They're not in the business of telling people what they want to hear."
-> hub

=== now
"Now?" He looks at the sky the way he'd look at entrails, without much hope. "Now the war comes to everyone. Even here. Even to people who voted against it." He gets up, knees cracking. "Go and do something useful. The gods will be busy."
-> hub
